  "notes": "patter: Northern lapwing (peewit): a pigeon-sized plover of low wet pasture and short-grass meadow, black and white at a distance, with a long wispy crest swept up off the back of its head and a back of dark green that flashes green and purple when the sun catches it (its fourth colour value below zero is iridescence). Long pinkish legs; run, stop, tip forward to peck, in loose flocks out on the open turf; flushed, the flock goes up on broad round-ended wings with slow floppy beats and comes down again a field away.",
